# Article and post artwork. It lives on GitHub because published writing links
# to it by raw URL, but it is not part of the package and pub warns about the
# plural directory name, so it stays out of the archive.
docs/

# The rest of this file exists because a .pubignore replaces .gitignore for the
# directory it sits in rather than adding to it. The moment the entry above was
# added, everything the root .gitignore excludes stopped being excluded from
# the archive, silently. Measured: with a build/ directory present, `dart pub
# publish --dry-run` packed it.
#
# pub skips .dart_tool/ and dot-directories on its own, so only build/ actually
# leaked, and only when a build had been run before publishing. Keep this list
# a superset of .gitignore anyway; the failure is invisible until an archive
# ships heavier than the package.
build/
pubspec.lock
.dart_tool/
.idea/
data/
